    <h2>Why slab leaks show up so often here</h2>
    <p>Richardson's older neighborhoods sit on the same shifting Blackland Prairie clay found across North Texas, and homes built during the 1960s-70s tract boom often still have their original supply lines running under the slab. That combination is why slab leak repair, not just drain clearing, is a routine call for plumbers working this city.</p>
