  <section><h2>Frequently asked questions about plumbers in Richardson</h2>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Who is the best plumber in Richardson, TX?</h3><p>For 2026, our top pick is Koen Plumbing, Inc., headquartered on N. Bowser Road in Richardson and operating continuously since 1946. Dean's Plumbing, also Richardson-based, is a strong second option as a family owned and operated shop with its own local address.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Why do Richardson homes get so many slab leaks?</h3><p>Much of Richardson's housing stock dates to the 1960s and 70s, built on expansive Blackland Prairie clay that expands and contracts with moisture. Original galvanized and cast-iron supply lines running under those slabs are now decades past their expected service life, which is why slab leaks are a routine plumbing call here.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Do I need a licensed plumber for repairs in Richardson?</h3><p>Yes. Texas requires plumbing work to be performed by a licensed plumber or under one's direct supervision. Ask any company for its Texas Master Plumber or Journeyman license number directly — two of the five we checked publish theirs plainly on their own sites.</p></div>
